---
import Img from '../../components/Img.astro';
import Default from '../../layouts/Default.astro';
---

<Default
	title="About me"
	description="Who I am: a developer from Prague at MONETA Money Bank, Applied Informatics student at VŠE, working on C++ and Linux performance on the side."
	seoKeywords="about me, background"
	current="About"
>
	<h1 class="page-title">About me</h1>
	<div class="about">
		<figure class="about-figure">
			<Img
				class="about-photo"
				src="/assets/img/about-me-photo-above-the-clouds.jpg"
				widths={[256, 352, 704]}
				sizes="(max-width: 48rem) 8rem, 22rem"
				alt="Tomáš Diblík sitting on a rock above the clouds at sunrise"
				fetchpriority="high"
			/>
			<figcaption>Madeira, sunrise near the PR1 trail</figcaption>
		</figure>
		<div class="about-text">
			<p>
				Hi, I'm Tomáš Diblík (male, 2005, currently in Prague). I've been shipping production software since 2020. Right now I work as a
				Developer at
				<a href="https://www.moneta.cz/">MONETA Money Bank</a> (mostly frontend in TypeScript and React, with some Java on the backend) and I
				study Applied Informatics at VŠE (graduating in 2028).
			</p>

			<p>
				I prefer long-term work projects, which (unfortunately) can't be open sourced, but I write <a href="/pages/blog">blog posts</a>
				about the interesting parts. I love that the software I create makes people's day-to-day work easier, and I like it when they
				appreciate or constructively criticize it. To be honest, I get a really strong adrenaline rush every time a complex program I've spent
				months on finally runs correctly and fast.
			</p>

			<p>
				Outside of work, I like programming stuff just for fun. Lately it's mostly low-level performance work in C++ (that's where I want to
				grow), some embedded work, 3D printing, TUIs, or tools I wish existed.
			</p>

			<p>
				I also love to travel. To break the ice, ask me about Madeira, Albania, or driving a '97 Škoda Octavia with 350k km on the clock to
				the Netherlands for the tulip season, I've got some crazy stories from all of them.
			</p>

			<p>
				I've also done a couple of hackathons and taught a programming course, more on the
				<a href="/pages/work-experience#teaching-and-hackathons">Experience page</a>.
			</p>

			<p>English is my second language, so if you spot a mistake, please <a href="mailto:dibla.tomas@post.cz">let me know</a>.</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</Default>
